          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            Broadly a
            %em quantum logic circuit
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logic+circuit"} logic circuit
            but in the context of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+information+theory"} quantum information theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+computation"} quantum computation
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+logic"} linear logic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+type+theory"} linear type theory
            underlying
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+physics"} quantum physics
          %p
            In the context of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+computation"} quantum computation
            %em quantum circuit diagram
            (originally: “quantum computational network”,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Deutsch89"} Deutsch 1989
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagram"} string diagram
            (
            %a{:href => "#AbramskyCoecke04"}> Abramsky &amp; Coecke 2004
            ) in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite-dimensional+vector+spaces"} finite-dimensional
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+spaces"} Hilbert spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+logic+gate"} quantum gates
            mapping between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+quantum+states"} spaces of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pure+quantum+state"} pure
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+states"} quantum states
          %p
            A generic
            %em pure
            quantum circuit might look as follows:
          %div{:style => "margin: -20px 0px 10px 10px"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/QuantumCircuitScheme-221025c.jpg", :width => "600px"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              \&amp;lbrack;figure from
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/TQP"} Myers et al. 2023
          %p
            Here, for instance, the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gate"}> quantum gate
            ”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mn 34
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{34}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+operator"} linear operator
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H} \oplus \mathscr{H}
          %p
            Notice that the quantum circuit is understood to be the actual
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagram"} string diagram
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+transformation"} linear transformation
            which it encodes: The compositeness of the diagram encodes how (e.g. in which order) available
            = succeed "-operations" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gate"} quantum gate
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+computer"} quantum computer
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+computation"} quantum computation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+programming+language"} quantum programming language
            and one also speaks of the “quantum circuit model of quantum computation” (e.g.
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#NielsenChuang00"} Nielsen &amp; Chuang 2000, §II.4.6
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Miszczak11"} Miszczak 2011, §3
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#Miszczak12"} 2012, §4.3
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BenetiCasati18"} Beneti &amp; Casati 2018, §3.2
          %p
            Accordingly, many existing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+programming+languages"} quantum programming languages
            are actually
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain+specific+programming+languages"} domain specific programming languages
            for quantum circuits, and as such they are often
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain+specific+embedded+programming+language"} embedded
            into ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theories"} type theories
            (for instance
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quipper"} Quipper
            and
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QWIRE"} QWIRE
          %p
            Often the basic Hilbert space building block here is taken to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+space"} complex
            2-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension+of+a+vector+space"}> dimensional
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H} \,\coloneqq\, \mathbb{C}^2
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/q-bits"} q-bits
          %p
            Sometimes all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gates"} quantum gates
            involved, and hence also the resulting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composite
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+maps"} linear maps
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invertible"} invertible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reversible+computation"} reversible computation
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+operator"} unitary
            quantum state evolution in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
          %p
            But more generally and certainly in the broader context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+information+theory"} quantum information theory
            (such as in formulating the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+teleportation+protocol"} quantum teleportation protocol
            and similar), quantum circuits are admitted to also contain crucial
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mechanics"} classical
            = succeed "-interaction," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
          %ol#IBMResearchBlogGraphics
            %li
              %p
                %em>
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+measurement"}> quantum measurement
                  \-gates
                ,
            %li
              %p
                %em>
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+state+preparation"}> quantum state preparation
                  \-gates
                ,
            %li
              %p
                %em>
                  classically
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/controlled+quantum+gates"} controlled quantum gates
                \.
          %div{:style => "margin: -20px 0px 10px 10px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/IBMOnMidCircuitMeasurement.jpg", :width => "700px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                (example from
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.ibm.com/blogs/research/2021/02/quantum-mid-circuit-measurement/"} IBM Research Blog 2021/02
          %p
            Here
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+measurement"} quantum measurement
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reversible+computation"} reversible
            (due to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+state+collapse"} quantum state collapse
            involved) but also non-deterministic, meaning that it is not immediately represented by a fixed linear map at all – at least not between the original Hilbert spaces.
          %p
            One may model the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tuple"} tuple
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection+operators"} projection operators
            corresponding to the possible set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            of measurement outcomes as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
            between the original
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi.mathscript ℋ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H}
            and its
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+set"} indexed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            (one rare place where this is made explicit, albeit without comment, is
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Selinger04"} Selinger 2004
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "https://www.mathstat.dal.ca/~selinger/papers/qpl.pdf#page=39"} p. 39
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi meas
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℋ
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mphantom
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mo −
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo ⊕
                            %mrow
                              %mi b
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                              %mi B
                          %mi ℋ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi ψ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo ⊕
                            %mrow
                              %mi b
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                              %mi B
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %msub
                            %mi P
                            %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi ψ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  meas
                  \&amp;
                  \\colon
                  \&amp;
                  \\mathcal{H}
                  \&amp;
                  \\xrightarrow{\phantom{--}}
                  \&amp;
                  \\underset{
                  b \colon B
                  }{\oplus}
                  \\mathcal{H}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  \\vert \psi \rangle
                  \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                  \\underset{b \colon B}{\oplus}
                  \\,
                  P_{b} \vert \psi \rangle
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Therefore, as soon as these three operations crossing the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+physics"} classical
            = succeed "-boundary" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+physics"} quantum physics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagrams"} string diagrams
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite-dimensional+vector+space"} finite-dimensional
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HilbertSpaces"} HilbertSpaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+products"} tensor products
            also some kind of reflection of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sums"} direct sums
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces+of+quantum+states"} spaces of quantum states
          %p
            For a critical assessment of the (lack of) literature on this issue see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#GurevichBlass21"} Gurevich &amp; Blass 2021
          %p
            One approach for handling these more general quantum circuits is (
            %a{:href => "#AharonovKitaevNisan98"}> Aharonov, Kitaev &amp; Nisan 1998
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Selinger04"} Selinger 2004
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+probability+theory"} quantum probability theory
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+operations"} quantum operations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+quantum+states"} spaces of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mixed+quantum+states"} mixed quantum states
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagrams"} string diagrams
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completely+positive+maps"} completely positive maps
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+spaces"} convex spaces
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/density+matrices"} density matrices
          %p
            Other approaches for giving
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            for quantum circuits in this general sense have been proposed (and implemented) in the discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+programming+language"} quantum programming language
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quipper"} Quipper
            (see the references
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "Quipper#ReferencesDependentLinearTypesAndCategoricalSemantics"} there
            %a{:href => "necessity+and+possibility#ModalQuantumLogic"} Quantum Modal Logic
            in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+linear+type+theory"} dependent linear type theory
            is discussed at:
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+circuits+via+dependent+linear+types"} quantum circuits via dependent linear types
              \.
          %p
            These turn out to be related: From a suitably rich formulation of quantum circuits of pure states with measurement and classical control, the
            = succeed "-formulation" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/density+matrix"} density matrix
          %p
            At the time of writing (2021) most of the actual programming of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experimental
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+computers"} quantum computers
            is conceived through quantum circuit diagrams, while more high-level
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+programming+languages"} quantum programming languages
            are are awaiting the rise of more powerful quantum hardware.
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %h3#bell_state_preparation Bell state preparation
          %p
            In
            = succeed "-based" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/qbit"} qbit
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+computation"} quantum computation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bell+state"} Bell state
            is usually prepared via the following small quantum circuit consisting of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hadamard+gate"} Hadamard gate
            followed by a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+CNOT+gate"} quantum CNOT gate
          %div{:style => "margin: -20px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/BellStatePreparationCircuit-221026.jpg", :width => "750px"}/
          %h3#quantum_teleportation Quantum teleportation
          %p
            The standard (cf.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "Quipper#GLRSV13"} GLRSV13, p. 5
            = succeed "-form" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/qbit"} qbit
            = succeed "-protocol" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+teleportation"} quantum teleportation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/qbits"} qbits
            (where “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            ” denotes the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hadamard+gate"} Hadamard gate
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+CNOT+gates"} quantum CNOT gates
            and the boxed pointers denote
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+measurement"} quantum measurement
            in the
            = succeed "-basis):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/qbit"} qbit
          %div{:style => "margin: -20px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/QBitQuantumTeleportationProtocol-221026.jpg", :width => "800px"}/
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#deferred_measurement_principle Deferred measurement principle
          %p
            See at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deferred+measurement+principle"} deferred measurement principle
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logic+circuit"} logic circuit
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QRAM"} QRAM
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+computation"}> quantum computation
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+error+correction"} quantum error correction
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagram"}> string diagram
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof+net"} proof net
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/DisCoPy"} DisCoPy
          %h2#references References
          %h3#quantum_circuit_diagrams Quantum circuit diagrams
          %p
            The notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gates"} quantum gates
            and quantum circuits acting on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pure+quantum+states"} pure quantum states
            originates with:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Feynman"}> Richard Feynman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum mechanical computers
                %strong 16
                (1986) 507–531 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01886518"}> doi:10.1007/BF01886518
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Deutsch89
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+E.+Deutsch"}> David E. Deutsch
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum computational networks
                %strong 425
                1868 (1989) 73-90 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1098/rspa.1989.0099"}> doi:10.1098/rspa.1989.0099
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2398494"} jstor:2398494
            %li#BBCDMSSSW95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adriano+Barenco"}> Adriano Barenco
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+H.+Bennett"} Charles H. Bennett
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Cleve"} Richard Cleve
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+P.+DiVincenzo"} David P. DiVincenzo
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Norman+Margolus"} Norman Margolus
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Shor"} Peter Shor
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tycho+Sleator"} Tycho Sleator
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+A.+Smolin"} John A. Smolin
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Harald+Weinfurter"} Harald Weinfurter
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Elementary gates for quantum computation
                %strong 52
                (1995) 3457 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/9503016"}> arXiv:quant-ph/9503016
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
