          %div
            %h3#quantum_programming_languages Quantum programming languages
            %p The first proposal towards formalizing quantum programming languages was:
            %ul
              %li#Knill96
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emanuel+Knill"}> Emanuel Knill
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Conventions for quantum pseudocode
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.osti.gov/biblio/366453-conventions-quantum-pseudocode"} LA-UR-96-2724
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2172/366453"} doi:10.2172/366453
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/366453"} pdf
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Knill-QuantumPseudocode.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %p
              and early formalization via
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+lambda-calculus"} quantum lambda-calculus
              invoking
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+logic"} linear logic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+type+theory"} linear types
              (cf.
              %a{:href => "#Pratt92"} Pratt 1992
              etc.):
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beno%C3%AEt+Valiron"}> Benoît Valiron
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em A functional programming language for quantum computation with classical control
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.20381/ruor-18372"} doi:10.20381/ruor-18372
